1
00:00:00,750 --> 00:00:04,587
[theme music playing]

2
00:00:11,010 --> 00:00:13,555
[Raul] <i>What if Arnaldo</i>
<i>really has a problem?</i>

3
00:00:13,638 --> 00:00:15,932
<i>How dare you say that to your own son?</i>

4
00:00:16,016 --> 00:00:18,435
<i>Someone is laughing,</i>
<i>and I have to stop it.</i>

5
00:00:18,518 --> 00:00:20,562
<i>No!</i>

6
00:00:20,645 --> 00:00:23,606
[Ivy] <i>If you could only see Arnaldo.</i>

7
00:00:23,690 --> 00:00:26,860
<i>All my plans are about to unfold.</i>

8
00:00:26,943 --> 00:00:30,155
<i>Whatever happened to Arnaldo,</i>
<i>I know you were behind it.</i>

9
00:00:30,238 --> 00:00:32,115
<i>-Be careful.</i>
<i>-I am being cautious.</i>

10
00:00:32,198 --> 00:00:35,243
<i>Slowly but surely, my plans are unfolding.</i>

11
00:00:35,326 --> 00:00:36,536
<i>But this isn't the end of it.</i>

12
00:00:36,619 --> 00:00:37,787
<i>What more will you do?</i>

13
00:00:37,871 --> 00:00:39,539
[man] <i>Twenty million pesos, Mayor.</i>

14
00:00:39,622 --> 00:00:42,417
<i>Bring it to the plaza within one hour.</i>

15
00:00:42,500 --> 00:00:46,546
<i>If you don't, Ivy Aguas will die.</i>

16
00:00:47,088 --> 00:00:48,339
<i>Ivy!</i>

17
00:00:48,423 --> 00:00:50,759
<i>I will not be threatened by nobody.</i>

18
00:00:50,842 --> 00:00:51,718
[screams]

19
00:00:51,801 --> 00:00:53,553
<i>The Ardientes are desperate</i>
<i>to work with you.</i>

20
00:00:53,636 --> 00:00:55,055
<i>But Diego's group keeps pushing you away.</i>

21
00:00:55,138 --> 00:00:56,890
<i>I don't have to worry about that.</i>

22
00:00:56,973 --> 00:00:59,726
<i>That Madrigal. We need him in our group.</i>

23
00:00:59,809 --> 00:01:01,561
<i>You should work on that. Understood?</i>

24
00:01:01,644 --> 00:01:02,687
[goon] <i>Congressman, confirmed.</i>

25
00:01:02,771 --> 00:01:05,273
<i>Jaguar has been watching Diego's camp.</i>

26
00:01:05,356 --> 00:01:08,151
<i>Do you mean to tell me that Jaguar</i>

27
00:01:08,234 --> 00:01:10,278
<i>and that snot-nosed Diego are teaming up?</i>

28
00:01:10,361 --> 00:01:13,698
<i>What are you waiting for?</i>
<i>Bring me that man!</i>

29
00:01:14,491 --> 00:01:15,992
[Rufo] <i>Why did you bring me here?</i>

30
00:01:16,076 --> 00:01:17,869
<i>To break Jaguar's trust.</i>

31
00:01:17,952 --> 00:01:19,579
<i>Try to destroy his will.</i>

32
00:01:19,662 --> 00:01:22,540
<i>Congressman, you're</i>
<i>talking to the wrong man.</i>

33
00:01:23,083 --> 00:01:25,710
<i>Rufo, what is it going to be?</i>

34
00:01:28,338 --> 00:01:30,590
[Arnaldo] <i>Clara, prepare 20 million pesos.</i>

35
00:01:31,966 --> 00:01:33,009
[grunts]

36
00:01:36,638 --> 00:01:38,223
-Good afternoon.
-[crowd chants] Diego Torillo!

37
00:01:38,306 --> 00:01:39,641
How are you?

38
00:01:39,724 --> 00:01:41,100
-[supporters continue chanting]
-Good afternoon.

39
00:01:41,184 --> 00:01:44,145
[Anna] Don't forget to vote for Diego…

40
00:01:44,229 --> 00:01:46,523
-this coming election.
-Hello.

41
00:01:46,606 --> 00:01:48,650
Thank you. Thank you.

42
00:01:49,609 --> 00:01:50,735
Hello, everyone!

43
00:01:50,819 --> 00:01:53,238
-[Anna] This election…
-How are you, everyone?

44
00:01:53,321 --> 00:01:55,198
[Anna] Please don't forget.

45
00:01:55,281 --> 00:01:57,617
-How are you?
-[supporters continue chanting]

46
00:01:57,700 --> 00:01:59,035
Let's take a selfie.

47
00:01:59,119 --> 00:02:00,870
[supporters continue chanting]

48
00:02:00,954 --> 00:02:02,789
-Thank you.
-Hello, how are you?

49
00:02:02,872 --> 00:02:04,207
Can I hug you?

50
00:02:04,290 --> 00:02:07,043
[supporters continue chanting]

51
00:02:07,127 --> 00:02:09,796
[Emilia] Okay. Where is everybody?

52
00:02:09,879 --> 00:02:12,006
Where are Arnaldo and Ivy?

53
00:02:12,090 --> 00:02:14,342
They haven't been
answering my calls, ma'am.

54
00:02:14,425 --> 00:02:18,596
What?! Arnaldo can't be absent
from his own campaign!

55
00:02:18,680 --> 00:02:20,098
-[supporters] Diego Torillo!
-Hello. How are you?

56
00:02:20,181 --> 00:02:21,808
[supporters chanting] Vote for change!

57
00:02:21,891 --> 00:02:22,934
How are you?

58
00:02:23,017 --> 00:02:25,103
Hi, sir. How are you doing?

59
00:02:25,186 --> 00:02:27,063
[supporters chanting] Vote for Diego!

60
00:02:27,147 --> 00:02:29,983
[Anna] Don't forget to vote for Diego!

61
00:02:30,066 --> 00:02:31,526
-Vote for change!
-Thank you.

62
00:02:31,609 --> 00:02:34,946
[supporters] Vote for Diego!
Vote for change!

63
00:02:35,029 --> 00:02:36,781
We can't fall behind schedule.

64
00:02:36,865 --> 00:02:38,783
-I know!
-Honestly, just cancel it.

65
00:02:38,867 --> 00:02:41,077
Emilia and I can't go there alone.

66
00:02:41,578 --> 00:02:43,163
You know, Auntie, you have a point.

67
00:02:43,580 --> 00:02:45,123
-Cancel it.
-Yes, ma'am.

68
00:02:45,206 --> 00:02:47,959
But, we're still pushing
through with our errand.

69
00:02:48,042 --> 00:02:50,670
[tense music playing]

70
00:02:53,381 --> 00:02:56,092
[ominous music playing]

71
00:03:02,724 --> 00:03:03,892
[gasps]

72
00:03:09,939 --> 00:03:11,065
[groans]

73
00:03:13,943 --> 00:03:15,862
[grunts]

74
00:03:19,949 --> 00:03:21,284
[exhales]

75
00:03:23,202 --> 00:03:24,120
Ivy?

76
00:03:28,416 --> 00:03:29,584
Ivy!

77
00:03:31,294 --> 00:03:32,378
Hey!

78
00:03:33,379 --> 00:03:34,964
Whoever you are, show yourself!

79
00:03:36,299 --> 00:03:37,383
[man] Give me my money first!

80
00:03:37,467 --> 00:03:39,719
[ominous music playing]

81
00:03:42,889 --> 00:03:44,307
Show me Ivy first!

82
00:03:45,516 --> 00:03:46,893
[man laughs]

83
00:03:47,518 --> 00:03:50,980
[man] You never stopped
being arrogant, did you?

84
00:03:51,064 --> 00:03:52,065
[scoffs]

85
00:03:52,690 --> 00:03:55,818
You, the Prince of the Ardientes.

86
00:03:56,861 --> 00:03:58,529
But where's your grandfather now?

87
00:03:58,988 --> 00:04:00,365
How about your money?

88
00:04:01,157 --> 00:04:03,243
How about your power? Your weapons?

89
00:04:04,077 --> 00:04:05,286
They're gone!

90
00:04:06,412 --> 00:04:08,248
The only ones here right now…

91
00:04:08,706 --> 00:04:11,084
are me and you!

92
00:04:12,293 --> 00:04:14,796
And today is the day you will fall.

93
00:04:14,879 --> 00:04:17,215
[tense music playing]

94
00:04:17,298 --> 00:04:18,716
[laughs]

95
00:04:19,884 --> 00:04:22,136
[laughs maniacally]

96
00:04:23,012 --> 00:04:24,180
Oh, please.

97
00:04:25,807 --> 00:04:27,100
Where are you?

98
00:04:27,809 --> 00:04:29,644
Why don't you come out and show your face?

99
00:04:30,436 --> 00:04:32,438
Oh, I know.

100
00:04:32,981 --> 00:04:34,524
You're just being chicken.

101
00:04:35,692 --> 00:04:36,985
Have it your way.

102
00:04:37,610 --> 00:04:38,695
Chicken!

103
00:04:39,696 --> 00:04:40,905
Chicken!

104
00:04:40,989 --> 00:04:42,615
[laughs]

105
00:04:43,074 --> 00:04:43,992
Chicken!

106
00:04:44,075 --> 00:04:46,536
[suspenseful music playing]

107
00:04:47,078 --> 00:04:48,705
[laughs]

108
00:04:49,872 --> 00:04:51,165
Hey, Mayor.

109
00:04:51,666 --> 00:04:54,002
[dramatic music]

110
00:04:54,085 --> 00:04:55,336
What's up?

111
00:04:55,420 --> 00:04:58,089
[tense music playing]

112
00:05:05,763 --> 00:05:08,182
[screams]

113
00:05:08,266 --> 00:05:10,935
[tense music playing]

114
00:05:15,356 --> 00:05:21,571
[chanting] Diego Torillo!
Vote for change now!

115
00:05:21,654 --> 00:05:28,036
-[unsettling music playing]
-[supporters continue chanting]

116
00:05:28,453 --> 00:05:31,956
[chanting] Diego Torillo!
Vote for change now!

117
00:05:32,040 --> 00:05:35,335
[supporters continue chanting]

118
00:05:38,755 --> 00:05:41,632
[Diego] <i>Ivy, why aren't you</i>
<i>here at the campaign?</i>

119
00:05:41,716 --> 00:05:43,426
<i>Arnaldo isn't here, either.</i>

120
00:05:43,509 --> 00:05:45,511
<i>Is something wrong?</i>

121
00:05:45,595 --> 00:05:48,389
[tense music playing]

122
00:05:50,183 --> 00:05:51,559
Where are they?

123
00:05:53,436 --> 00:05:54,812
Diego, is something wrong?

124
00:05:56,189 --> 00:05:57,482
Where's Ivy?

125
00:05:59,067 --> 00:06:00,860
It's nothing. Let's go.

126
00:06:00,943 --> 00:06:03,321
[tense music playing]

127
00:06:06,491 --> 00:06:07,992
Mr. Torillo, I'm glad you made it.

128
00:06:08,618 --> 00:06:10,036
Where are the Ardientes?

129
00:06:10,119 --> 00:06:12,538
Mayor Arnaldo's camp canceled,

130
00:06:12,622 --> 00:06:14,624
but you can proceed with your campaign.

131
00:06:14,707 --> 00:06:15,541
All right?

132
00:06:15,625 --> 00:06:17,168
-Excuse me.
-Thank you.

133
00:06:17,710 --> 00:06:20,797
[Marlon] Batch, I think the
Ardientes are up to something.

134
00:06:22,465 --> 00:06:23,424
This isn't good.

135
00:06:23,883 --> 00:06:26,886
[tense music playing]

136
00:06:36,479 --> 00:06:38,481
-Good morning.
-Good morning, ma'am.

137
00:06:38,564 --> 00:06:41,692
It'll get even better
so proceed as planned.

138
00:06:41,776 --> 00:06:43,111
Yes, ma'am.

139
00:06:43,194 --> 00:06:46,072
[ominous music playing]

140
00:06:47,031 --> 00:06:49,200
DIEGO FOR THE NEW ARDIENTE

141
00:06:55,998 --> 00:06:57,333
[Diego] <i>Hello, everyone!</i>

142
00:06:57,416 --> 00:07:00,169
Thank you for coming here today.

143
00:07:00,253 --> 00:07:02,004
I want to introduce myself to you.

144
00:07:02,088 --> 00:07:04,966
I am Diego Torillo.

145
00:07:05,550 --> 00:07:07,802
I am running for governor of this town.

146
00:07:07,885 --> 00:07:09,720
[cheering and applause]

147
00:07:09,804 --> 00:07:12,473
We will be giving away a few supplies.

148
00:07:12,557 --> 00:07:14,183
-[supporters chanting]
-I hope it helps.

149
00:07:14,267 --> 00:07:16,310
Line up over here, please.

150
00:07:16,394 --> 00:07:17,645
This is for you.

151
00:07:17,728 --> 00:07:19,605
[supporters chanting] Diego Torillo!

152
00:07:20,940 --> 00:07:22,859
[chuckles]

153
00:07:25,194 --> 00:07:28,197
-[supporters chanting]
-Thank you.

154
00:07:28,281 --> 00:07:31,784
Diego Torillo for real change!

155
00:07:32,410 --> 00:07:33,828
[Anna] Diego!

156
00:07:33,911 --> 00:07:36,080
-[supporters continue chanting]
-[ominous music playing]

157
00:07:36,164 --> 00:07:37,498
Over here.

158
00:07:38,749 --> 00:07:40,751
[Claire] Emilia, stop this already.

159
00:07:41,210 --> 00:07:42,795
You're violating your peace agreement

160
00:07:42,879 --> 00:07:44,422
with Diego's camp.

161
00:07:44,505 --> 00:07:48,426
Auntie, this is an unelaborate carnage.

162
00:07:48,509 --> 00:07:50,636
This won't hurt so bad.

163
00:07:50,720 --> 00:07:52,305
[supporters] Diego Torillo!

164
00:07:52,388 --> 00:07:53,723
Just stand here and wait in line.

165
00:07:53,806 --> 00:07:56,559
There's enough for everyone.

166
00:07:57,226 --> 00:07:59,061
Come with me
if you don't want to get hurt.

167
00:07:59,145 --> 00:08:00,396
Don't scream.

168
00:08:00,855 --> 00:08:03,691
[supporters] Diego Torillo
for real change!

169
00:08:03,774 --> 00:08:05,902
-Come on.
-Diego Torillo!

170
00:08:05,985 --> 00:08:07,445
[Claire] Goodness, Emilia.

171
00:08:07,528 --> 00:08:09,322
What will you get out of this?

172
00:08:09,405 --> 00:08:12,992
Well, Auntie, I want
to show Miss Lily Cruz

173
00:08:13,075 --> 00:08:14,660
that I can embarrass her

174
00:08:14,744 --> 00:08:16,829
the same way she embarrassed me.

175
00:08:16,913 --> 00:08:21,334
But she'll get a lot worse.

176
00:08:22,293 --> 00:08:23,669
I'll make sure of that.

177
00:08:23,753 --> 00:08:26,047
[ominous music playing]

178
00:08:28,382 --> 00:08:30,510
-[supporters chanting]
-Let go of me!

179
00:08:30,593 --> 00:08:32,678
[chuckles]

180
00:08:32,762 --> 00:08:35,223
This is just so exciting, Auntie.

181
00:08:35,306 --> 00:08:38,935
Diego Torillo for a new Ardiente!

182
00:08:39,018 --> 00:08:40,394
[chanting] Diego Torillo…

183
00:08:40,478 --> 00:08:42,104
Batch, it's Lily!

184
00:08:43,814 --> 00:08:44,857
It's Lily!

185
00:08:45,775 --> 00:08:46,984
Move!

186
00:08:47,068 --> 00:08:48,194
Lily!

187
00:08:48,861 --> 00:08:50,655
-[Lily grunts]
-Come here!

188
00:08:52,198 --> 00:08:53,491
-Hurry up!
-Hey!

189
00:08:53,574 --> 00:08:54,784
Hey!

190
00:08:57,578 --> 00:08:58,704
Where are you taking me?!

191
00:08:58,788 --> 00:09:00,414
-Come on!
-Let me go!

192
00:09:00,498 --> 00:09:02,750
[tense music playing]

193
00:09:03,751 --> 00:09:06,003
Are you going to kill us?!

194
00:09:12,301 --> 00:09:14,011
Danny, give me that!

195
00:09:14,095 --> 00:09:15,471
-[screaming]
-[grunts]

196
00:09:15,555 --> 00:09:16,806
Shoot!

197
00:09:22,812 --> 00:09:23,813
Diego!

198
00:09:23,896 --> 00:09:25,690
Diego, be careful!

199
00:09:25,773 --> 00:09:27,900
Who sent you?!

200
00:09:27,984 --> 00:09:29,902
-Answer me!
-[whistles]

201
00:09:29,986 --> 00:09:30,945
There!

202
00:09:31,028 --> 00:09:32,530
Get him out of here.

203
00:09:33,072 --> 00:09:35,199
What are you waiting for?!
This isn't a movie!

204
00:09:35,283 --> 00:09:36,993
Drive! Let's go!

205
00:09:37,076 --> 00:09:39,704
[tense music playing]

206
00:09:44,333 --> 00:09:45,793
Mr. Diego, that's enough.

207
00:09:49,839 --> 00:09:50,923
[Marlon] Diego!

208
00:09:51,007 --> 00:09:53,009
-[Anna] Diego, it's over.
-[Marlon] Let them do their job!

209
00:09:55,303 --> 00:09:57,555
[indistinct chatter]

210
00:09:57,638 --> 00:09:58,556
Are you okay, Batch?

211
00:09:58,639 --> 00:10:00,641
-Lily, are you hurt?!
-Are you okay?

212
00:10:00,725 --> 00:10:02,768
-How about you?
-I'm fine.

213
00:10:04,937 --> 00:10:08,399
-Thank you, Diego.
-They're okay. Thanks.

214
00:10:08,482 --> 00:10:10,067
[indistinct chatter]

215
00:10:12,612 --> 00:10:13,571
[woman] Arrest him!

216
00:10:15,698 --> 00:10:19,160
I'm sure the Ardientes are behind this.

217
00:10:19,243 --> 00:10:22,246
[tense music playing]

218
00:10:24,707 --> 00:10:26,876
[ominous music playing]

219
00:10:28,502 --> 00:10:30,504
How have you been, Mayor?

220
00:10:32,757 --> 00:10:33,924
[laughs]

221
00:10:34,884 --> 00:10:36,552
It's been a while!

222
00:10:40,014 --> 00:10:42,975
How are things, Mayor?

223
00:10:44,185 --> 00:10:45,186
You know what?

224
00:10:46,687 --> 00:10:48,522
I want to applaud you
for your grand entrance,

225
00:10:48,606 --> 00:10:50,358
but I'm all tied up.

226
00:10:50,775 --> 00:10:52,234
How's business doing?

227
00:10:53,486 --> 00:10:55,321
Business is doing well.

228
00:10:55,738 --> 00:10:57,448
But, seriously, what are you high on?

229
00:10:59,158 --> 00:11:00,660
You think you'll get away with this?

230
00:11:01,702 --> 00:11:04,622
A lunatic like you won't.

231
00:11:05,748 --> 00:11:07,458
You were the psycho
in the town square, right?

232
00:11:10,086 --> 00:11:11,337
Psycho.

233
00:11:11,879 --> 00:11:13,089
That's right.

234
00:11:14,965 --> 00:11:16,926
[laughs]

235
00:11:17,009 --> 00:11:18,469
Where's Ivy?

236
00:11:19,762 --> 00:11:23,224
-Where is she?!
-That she-devil?

237
00:11:23,808 --> 00:11:26,352
She's on her way to hell!

238
00:11:29,146 --> 00:11:30,648
You're all the same…

239
00:11:31,482 --> 00:11:36,320
You may have money,
but you're all just evil!

240
00:11:36,404 --> 00:11:39,448
You're all bad people,
and you're going to hell!

241
00:11:39,532 --> 00:11:41,826
[ominous music playing]

242
00:11:42,952 --> 00:11:46,080
You want money, right? Twenty million?

243
00:11:46,747 --> 00:11:50,292
You won't get your money until I get Ivy.

244
00:11:51,419 --> 00:11:52,545
Where is she?!

245
00:11:52,628 --> 00:11:54,713
[grunts]

246
00:11:54,797 --> 00:11:56,382
That's not going to happen!

247
00:11:58,509 --> 00:12:00,553
Give me my money,

248
00:12:00,636 --> 00:12:03,180
and I'll tell you where she is.

249
00:12:03,264 --> 00:12:04,640
[scoffs]

250
00:12:04,723 --> 00:12:05,933
But if you don't…

251
00:12:06,016 --> 00:12:08,102
[labored breathing]

252
00:12:10,187 --> 00:12:12,064
You won't find her alive,

253
00:12:12,148 --> 00:12:13,816
and she's going straight to hell!

254
00:12:13,899 --> 00:12:15,776
You can all burn down there together!

255
00:12:17,695 --> 00:12:18,863
[scoffs]

256
00:12:20,948 --> 00:12:22,825
Oh, right!

257
00:12:25,119 --> 00:12:27,329
She wanted me to give you this.

258
00:12:30,833 --> 00:12:31,959
Here.

259
00:12:34,879 --> 00:12:36,464
You bastard!

260
00:12:36,547 --> 00:12:37,756
Where is she?!

261
00:12:37,840 --> 00:12:40,801
Let me see her! What did you do to her?!

262
00:12:40,885 --> 00:12:42,511
I'm going to kill you!

263
00:12:42,595 --> 00:12:45,639
I'll kill you! I'll kill you!

264
00:12:45,723 --> 00:12:47,558
-Let her go!
-Wait!

265
00:12:47,641 --> 00:12:48,893
[laughs]

266
00:12:49,768 --> 00:12:52,188
-You bastard!
-You should see yourself!

267
00:12:52,271 --> 00:12:53,147
[grunts]

268
00:12:54,064 --> 00:12:57,109
I'm going to kill you!
I'm going to kill you!

269
00:12:57,193 --> 00:12:59,236
Who's the psycho now?

270
00:12:59,320 --> 00:13:01,197
[labored breathing]

271
00:13:01,280 --> 00:13:04,033
[laughing]

272
00:13:18,964 --> 00:13:20,966
If you just brought the money with you,

273
00:13:21,592 --> 00:13:23,344
we wouldn't have a problem now.

274
00:13:26,764 --> 00:13:28,724
I'm actually surprised, Mayor.

275
00:13:30,893 --> 00:13:33,604
Aren't you generous?

276
00:13:34,271 --> 00:13:38,734
Because your family is the
richest and greediest of all!

277
00:13:40,194 --> 00:13:41,529
Mayor.

278
00:13:44,907 --> 00:13:46,242
Mayor.

279
00:13:48,077 --> 00:13:49,495
Twenty million?

280
00:13:50,162 --> 00:13:51,330
[scoffs]

281
00:13:51,413 --> 00:13:53,040
That's nothing, right?

282
00:13:53,123 --> 00:13:55,167
There's one thing I'm curious about.

283
00:13:56,877 --> 00:13:58,671
Why are you after the money now?

284
00:13:59,213 --> 00:14:00,965
-Weren't you an activist?
-[sighs]

285
00:14:01,048 --> 00:14:03,759
You even testified against my family.

286
00:14:04,385 --> 00:14:07,221
Am I right? Answer me.

287
00:14:09,098 --> 00:14:10,224
[sighs]

288
00:14:11,308 --> 00:14:12,309
Yes.

289
00:14:14,728 --> 00:14:16,939
But what happened to the other witnesses?

290
00:14:17,773 --> 00:14:19,191
What happened to them?

291
00:14:19,275 --> 00:14:20,818
Of course, I had them killed!

292
00:14:22,778 --> 00:14:25,406
I even killed the others myself.

293
00:14:30,160 --> 00:14:31,370
[laughs]

294
00:14:33,372 --> 00:14:35,875
[laughs maniacally]

295
00:14:37,001 --> 00:14:38,168
This only proves…

296
00:14:39,420 --> 00:14:41,964
there's no place for justice in Ardiente!

297
00:14:43,340 --> 00:14:44,675
What do we have instead?

298
00:14:45,217 --> 00:14:46,427
Violence.

299
00:14:47,011 --> 00:14:48,178
Bloodshed.

300
00:14:49,889 --> 00:14:50,973
And wealth!

301
00:14:51,807 --> 00:14:53,017
That's all!

302
00:14:53,809 --> 00:14:56,645
And that's what I'm going
to take from you!

303
00:14:56,729 --> 00:14:59,857
[tense music playing]

304
00:15:04,278 --> 00:15:05,779
Thank goodness you're safe

305
00:15:05,863 --> 00:15:07,656
despite what Emilia did to you.

306
00:15:07,740 --> 00:15:10,659
Yes, Auntie Camia.
Good thing Diego was there.

307
00:15:11,744 --> 00:15:13,078
My goodness.

308
00:15:13,162 --> 00:15:15,414
I suddenly got worried about Lily.

309
00:15:15,497 --> 00:15:18,918
I've been texting her,
but she hasn't replied yet.

310
00:15:19,001 --> 00:15:21,879
Maybe she just went
somewhere with Arnaldo.

311
00:15:22,296 --> 00:15:26,008
They might be busy
preparing for their wedding.

312
00:15:26,800 --> 00:15:28,469
But I feel that something's wrong.

313
00:15:29,011 --> 00:15:32,264
I'm a mother so I can sense it
if my daughter is in danger.

314
00:15:33,766 --> 00:15:35,309
Don't worry too much.

315
00:15:35,726 --> 00:15:37,728
Ivy can take care of herself.

316
00:15:38,687 --> 00:15:40,439
I'm sure she knows what she's doing.

317
00:15:42,775 --> 00:15:45,194
I just want to make sure
she's safe all the time.

318
00:15:45,277 --> 00:15:47,279
I want to know what she's up to.

319
00:15:48,697 --> 00:15:49,949
We all do.

320
00:15:50,199 --> 00:15:52,743
[somber music playing]

321
00:16:00,709 --> 00:16:01,919
So, Mayor…

322
00:16:02,002 --> 00:16:05,297
Where's my 20 million pesos?!

323
00:16:06,966 --> 00:16:08,759
Mayor!

324
00:16:10,094 --> 00:16:12,054
[sighs] Where is it?!

325
00:16:12,972 --> 00:16:17,601
Can we please stop prolonging this?!

326
00:16:17,685 --> 00:16:20,104
Where is it? Where is it?!

327
00:16:21,689 --> 00:16:24,233
Where is Ivy?!

328
00:16:24,775 --> 00:16:26,402
I want to see her.

329
00:16:26,485 --> 00:16:27,903
What if you don't?!

330
00:16:28,487 --> 00:16:29,822
You won't have your money!

331
00:16:31,657 --> 00:16:33,867
Then you won't ever see Ivy again.

332
00:16:33,951 --> 00:16:36,996
[both chuckle]

333
00:16:37,079 --> 00:16:40,499
Do you think that I believe
anything you say?!

334
00:16:41,083 --> 00:16:42,626
You don't have Ivy!

335
00:16:42,710 --> 00:16:45,212
Everything you said was a lie!

336
00:16:45,295 --> 00:16:47,006
Ivy isn't here!

337
00:16:47,089 --> 00:16:49,425
She's not here!

338
00:16:49,508 --> 00:16:51,760
Oh, a gun!

339
00:16:53,262 --> 00:16:55,222
Do you think you can scare me with that?

340
00:16:55,305 --> 00:16:56,640
Ivy's not here!

341
00:16:56,724 --> 00:16:59,643
If she was here,
you would've shown her to me!

342
00:16:59,727 --> 00:17:00,769
But no!

343
00:17:00,853 --> 00:17:02,980
No money, no Ivy!

344
00:17:03,063 --> 00:17:04,690
Nothing!

345
00:17:04,773 --> 00:17:07,985
[whispers] Nothing! Nothing. Nothing.

346
00:17:08,068 --> 00:17:10,738
[heavy breathing]

347
00:17:14,074 --> 00:17:16,076
-Nothing?
-Nothing.

348
00:17:23,417 --> 00:17:24,752
[line rings]

349
00:17:24,835 --> 00:17:25,961
Hello!

350
00:17:27,087 --> 00:17:31,675
Put Ivy Aguas on the phone.

351
00:17:33,510 --> 00:17:34,636
Now!

352
00:17:34,720 --> 00:17:37,222
[unsettling music playing]

353
00:17:40,309 --> 00:17:41,310
[Arthur exhales sharply]

354
00:17:42,311 --> 00:17:43,395
Hello!

355
00:17:43,854 --> 00:17:45,064
[laughs]

356
00:17:45,147 --> 00:17:46,273
Ivy!

357
00:17:47,274 --> 00:17:48,358
So…

358
00:17:49,860 --> 00:17:52,196
You're still alive there, huh?

359
00:17:53,072 --> 00:17:55,407
Someone wants to talk to you.

360
00:17:56,325 --> 00:17:59,328
Should I put him on the line?

361
00:18:00,788 --> 00:18:02,664
Answer me, Miss Aguas!

362
00:18:04,208 --> 00:18:06,710
-[laughs] No one's on the line.
-There…

363
00:18:06,794 --> 00:18:08,337
[laughs]

364
00:18:08,420 --> 00:18:10,964
[ominous music playing]

365
00:18:14,301 --> 00:18:15,344
Ivy?

366
00:18:15,427 --> 00:18:19,223
[muffled screaming] Hon! Hon!

367
00:18:19,306 --> 00:18:20,599
Ivy!

368
00:18:21,308 --> 00:18:23,310
-Hon!
-<i>What did they do-- Ivy!</i>

369
00:18:24,686 --> 00:18:26,105
You bastard! Let her go!

370
00:18:26,188 --> 00:18:27,356
I'll give you everything.

371
00:18:27,439 --> 00:18:29,900
I'll give you everything, just let her go.

372
00:18:30,692 --> 00:18:32,486
[muffled screaming]

373
00:18:33,695 --> 00:18:35,948
[sobbing] Hon!

374
00:18:36,281 --> 00:18:39,118
Hon! [whimpers]

375
00:18:41,870 --> 00:18:43,205
[phone clatters]

376
00:18:45,374 --> 00:18:48,001
The Ardientes are all devious!

377
00:18:49,503 --> 00:18:51,213
[laughs]

378
00:18:52,965 --> 00:18:55,008
-Wait--
-How can I be sure…

379
00:18:55,092 --> 00:18:57,219
that you'll give me everything I want?

380
00:18:58,178 --> 00:19:01,515
I can even buy your soul, you idiot.

381
00:19:03,642 --> 00:19:05,978
But you know what else I can do?

382
00:19:06,061 --> 00:19:08,522
[suspenseful music playing]

383
00:19:11,733 --> 00:19:13,694
[grunts]

384
00:19:15,028 --> 00:19:17,114
[groans]

385
00:19:19,366 --> 00:19:20,701
[grunts]

386
00:19:22,494 --> 00:19:23,996
What now?!

387
00:19:24,079 --> 00:19:27,124
Stand up! Come here!

388
00:19:27,207 --> 00:19:28,333
[grunts]

389
00:19:28,417 --> 00:19:30,711
[tense music playing]

390
00:19:35,591 --> 00:19:36,758
What now, Arthur?

391
00:19:37,384 --> 00:19:39,595
I always get what I want!

392
00:19:40,846 --> 00:19:43,932
So give me back my fiancée
before I blow your brains out.

393
00:19:44,600 --> 00:19:45,893
[grunts]

394
00:19:56,445 --> 00:19:57,738
[grunts]

395
00:19:58,697 --> 00:19:59,698
Go ahead!

396
00:20:01,366 --> 00:20:02,701
[laughs]

397
00:20:04,286 --> 00:20:05,662
What now, huh?

398
00:20:06,663 --> 00:20:10,584
You Ardientes really are something else.

399
00:20:11,126 --> 00:20:13,378
You all think you're so high and mighty.

400
00:20:14,713 --> 00:20:15,923
So, Mayor…

401
00:20:17,090 --> 00:20:18,508
Take it from me.

402
00:20:20,886 --> 00:20:23,805
I think Carlotta and Nimfa are
calling you to the other side.

403
00:20:24,181 --> 00:20:25,724
They might even pay you a visit.

404
00:20:25,807 --> 00:20:27,726
Each and every one of you!

405
00:20:28,560 --> 00:20:30,062
Are you messing with me?

406
00:20:33,815 --> 00:20:35,192
Are you messing with me?

407
00:20:35,275 --> 00:20:36,318
Mayor…

408
00:20:36,401 --> 00:20:37,527
You're messing--

409
00:20:37,611 --> 00:20:40,322
Think twice about everything
you're going to do.

410
00:20:41,740 --> 00:20:46,995
You don't want to marry
a corpse now, do you?

411
00:20:47,079 --> 00:20:49,498
[tense music playing]

412
00:21:00,676 --> 00:21:01,677
My goodness, Emilia.

413
00:21:01,760 --> 00:21:03,845
You're being reckless again.

414
00:21:04,304 --> 00:21:07,933
Can you please just be still
and go with the flow?

415
00:21:08,016 --> 00:21:10,018
Strike when the right time comes.

416
00:21:10,102 --> 00:21:11,770
Like a crocodile, Auntie?

417
00:21:11,853 --> 00:21:13,522
That's too boring.

418
00:21:13,605 --> 00:21:15,232
Like they say, Auntie…

419
00:21:15,315 --> 00:21:17,234
you must try and try until--

420
00:21:17,317 --> 00:21:18,610
You die?

421
00:21:19,361 --> 00:21:23,282
Seriously, can you please
just be Julio's pawn for now?

422
00:21:24,199 --> 00:21:25,409
My goodness.

423
00:21:25,492 --> 00:21:28,870
I don't know what I'd do
if something happens to you.

424
00:21:29,788 --> 00:21:31,290
Don't worry, Auntie.

425
00:21:31,373 --> 00:21:33,917
That's really sweet of you.
Thank you for your concern.

426
00:21:34,001 --> 00:21:35,502
But if anyone's going to die here,

427
00:21:35,585 --> 00:21:37,421
it definitely won't be me.

428
00:21:37,504 --> 00:21:39,923
First, it'll be Lily Cruz.

429
00:21:40,007 --> 00:21:42,801
Then, Ivy Aguas, and then…

430
00:21:43,302 --> 00:21:44,720
Let's not mention the last one.

431
00:21:44,803 --> 00:21:46,471
It might just come true.

432
00:21:47,723 --> 00:21:48,765
[sighs]

433
00:21:49,391 --> 00:21:50,934
Relax, Auntie.

434
00:21:51,518 --> 00:21:52,477
[exhales]

435
00:21:56,148 --> 00:21:58,025
THE MONEY'S ALREADY
AT THE PICK-UP POINT.

436
00:21:59,276 --> 00:22:00,527
[laughs]

437
00:22:00,610 --> 00:22:02,029
Oh, here it is.

438
00:22:02,112 --> 00:22:06,116
Looks like I finally got
the money you sent.

439
00:22:06,491 --> 00:22:08,118
[laughs]

440
00:22:09,870 --> 00:22:10,662
Thanks.

441
00:22:10,746 --> 00:22:12,789
Great, you got what you wanted.

442
00:22:12,873 --> 00:22:13,749
Now, give me Ivy.

443
00:22:13,832 --> 00:22:15,792
-Now, now…
-I said give me Ivy!

444
00:22:15,876 --> 00:22:17,294
Shh…

445
00:22:18,587 --> 00:22:19,838
Now…

446
00:22:22,174 --> 00:22:23,342
Take this.

447
00:22:24,426 --> 00:22:26,511
You'll find Ivy Aguas here.

448
00:22:27,512 --> 00:22:28,680
Come on.

449
00:22:29,723 --> 00:22:30,724
Take it.

450
00:22:30,807 --> 00:22:32,976
[unsettling music playing]

451
00:22:34,478 --> 00:22:35,687
Come closer.

452
00:22:38,273 --> 00:22:39,274
Closer!

453
00:22:39,357 --> 00:22:42,069
[unsettling music continues]

454
00:22:45,363 --> 00:22:46,698
I said closer.

455
00:22:47,491 --> 00:22:50,327
Come on, just a little more.

456
00:22:50,869 --> 00:22:52,037
Don't be so shy.

457
00:22:52,996 --> 00:22:54,122
Come on.

458
00:22:54,498 --> 00:22:55,791
You're so close.

459
00:22:56,166 --> 00:22:57,501
Just a little more.

460
00:23:00,087 --> 00:23:01,296
[grunts]

461
00:23:02,506 --> 00:23:04,549
This is for torturing me back then!

462
00:23:04,633 --> 00:23:05,717
[grunts]

463
00:23:07,094 --> 00:23:12,015
And this is for what you
bastards did to my sibling!

464
00:23:12,099 --> 00:23:13,225
[grunts]

465
00:23:19,022 --> 00:23:21,566
This is revenge for all the
innocent lives you've killed!

466
00:23:22,609 --> 00:23:24,319
But, remember this, Mayor.

467
00:23:25,278 --> 00:23:26,530
I'm not alone!

468
00:23:27,864 --> 00:23:28,990
There are plenty more

469
00:23:29,991 --> 00:23:32,869
waiting in line to make you pay.

470
00:23:34,496 --> 00:23:37,999
You're lucky I'm a good man.

471
00:23:39,501 --> 00:23:41,628
And that I didn't kill your fiancée.

472
00:23:41,711 --> 00:23:44,464
[tense music playing]

473
00:23:54,808 --> 00:23:56,309
But you better hurry.

474
00:23:57,477 --> 00:23:59,437
Or you might not reach her alive.

475
00:23:59,980 --> 00:24:03,066
[tense music continues]

476
00:24:10,615 --> 00:24:15,287
You and Ivy Aguas
will be reunited in hell.

477
00:24:15,370 --> 00:24:18,498
[tense music playing]

478
00:24:34,723 --> 00:24:37,642
[unsettling music playing]

479
00:24:41,938 --> 00:24:42,939
Rufo!

480
00:24:46,776 --> 00:24:48,195
How'd you get inside?

481
00:24:52,407 --> 00:24:54,451
I know you met with Julio Ardiente.

482
00:24:56,077 --> 00:24:57,704
What did you two talk about?

483
00:24:57,787 --> 00:24:59,748
Will you sell Jaguar out?

484
00:24:59,831 --> 00:25:02,626
[unsettling music playing]

485
00:25:07,714 --> 00:25:08,882
Rufo.

486
00:25:09,507 --> 00:25:11,509
It's dangerous to work for two demons.

487
00:25:14,512 --> 00:25:18,183
Especially if one is an Ardiente.

488
00:25:20,018 --> 00:25:21,686
Too dangerous, actually.

489
00:25:24,606 --> 00:25:25,607
Why?

490
00:25:26,191 --> 00:25:27,776
Will you rat me out?

491
00:25:29,277 --> 00:25:30,612
Why not?

492
00:25:31,238 --> 00:25:32,197
[scoffs]

493
00:25:34,074 --> 00:25:35,200
Well then…

494
00:25:36,409 --> 00:25:37,619
I guess I have no choice!

495
00:25:37,702 --> 00:25:39,913
[tense music playing]

496
00:25:41,957 --> 00:25:43,083
You know what?

497
00:25:43,959 --> 00:25:45,460
You can work for me.

498
00:25:46,670 --> 00:25:50,173
Together, we'll manage
the Ardientes' gambling dens.

499
00:25:50,882 --> 00:25:53,218
I don't trust traitors like you, Rufo.

500
00:25:53,301 --> 00:25:54,970
[laughs]

501
00:25:56,304 --> 00:25:57,514
We both are.

502
00:25:58,890 --> 00:26:00,350
We aren't, Rufo.

503
00:26:01,393 --> 00:26:02,769
What you want is money.

504
00:26:03,895 --> 00:26:05,480
I want their lives.

505
00:26:06,773 --> 00:26:07,857
[grunts]

506
00:26:11,486 --> 00:26:12,862
[grunts]

507
00:26:23,498 --> 00:26:24,249
Let go!

508
00:26:24,332 --> 00:26:26,626
[action music playing]

509
00:26:33,758 --> 00:26:36,052
[grunts]

510
00:26:43,977 --> 00:26:44,978
Help me!

511
00:26:46,187 --> 00:26:47,647
Help!

512
00:26:49,065 --> 00:26:50,275
Help me!

513
00:26:52,485 --> 00:26:53,695
Help! Help!

514
00:26:54,195 --> 00:26:55,864
Kill him!

515
00:26:55,947 --> 00:26:57,574
He's one of the Ardientes' men!

516
00:26:57,949 --> 00:26:59,701
-Hurry up!
-Call your boss!

517
00:26:59,784 --> 00:27:01,161
He needs to learn the truth.

518
00:27:01,244 --> 00:27:03,288
-What are you waiting for?!
-Jaguar!

519
00:27:03,371 --> 00:27:05,206
-Jaguar!
-Come on, help me!

520
00:27:05,290 --> 00:27:08,084
[tense music playing]

521
00:27:16,092 --> 00:27:17,052
[sighs]

522
00:27:17,135 --> 00:27:19,721
[ominous music playing]

523
00:27:25,101 --> 00:27:26,728
[doctor] <i>Julio, I'm sorry…</i>

524
00:27:26,811 --> 00:27:28,897
<i>but your cancer is back.</i>

525
00:27:29,356 --> 00:27:32,025
<i>Bone cancer is very dangerous.</i>

526
00:27:32,609 --> 00:27:34,402
<i>Are you saying my days are numbered?</i>

527
00:27:35,070 --> 00:27:37,655
<i>Julio, we have to conduct more tests.</i>

528
00:27:38,281 --> 00:27:39,366
No!

529
00:27:40,617 --> 00:27:46,289
Neither this disease nor that
bastard Jaguar can kill me!

530
00:27:47,707 --> 00:27:50,710
Now that his right hand
is under my control,

531
00:27:52,003 --> 00:27:55,215
I'll know how to finish him off.

532
00:27:55,298 --> 00:27:57,801
[ominous music playing]

533
00:27:57,884 --> 00:28:00,929
<i>So, when we meet again,</i>

534
00:28:02,097 --> 00:28:05,642
<i>I expect you to bring</i>
<i>Jaguar's head with you.</i>

535
00:28:06,893 --> 00:28:08,103
<i>Of course I will, Julio.</i>

536
00:28:09,437 --> 00:28:13,691
<i>Like you, I also expect</i>
<i>the reward you promised.</i>

537
00:28:14,150 --> 00:28:17,529
<i>You'll give me all of Jaguar's</i>
<i>businesses when he's gone,</i>

538
00:28:18,613 --> 00:28:22,742
<i>and you'll appoint me to the</i>
<i>position you told me about.</i>

539
00:28:23,284 --> 00:28:24,911
[chuckles]

540
00:28:26,496 --> 00:28:29,332
<i>You know, I like ambitious people.</i>

541
00:28:30,333 --> 00:28:33,211
<i>Because they will do everything they can</i>

542
00:28:33,294 --> 00:28:36,631
<i>just to fulfill their dreams.</i>

543
00:28:36,714 --> 00:28:38,967
[ominous music playing]

544
00:28:58,987 --> 00:29:00,447
[groans]

545
00:29:03,616 --> 00:29:05,076
-Jaguar!
-Jaguar!

546
00:29:06,953 --> 00:29:09,289
-Kill him! Hurry up!
-Jaguar!

547
00:29:09,372 --> 00:29:10,790
-Jaguar!
-You need to know the truth.

548
00:29:10,874 --> 00:29:13,918
Jaguar, I caught him.

549
00:29:14,002 --> 00:29:16,171
He's one of the Ardientes' men. Kill him!

550
00:29:16,880 --> 00:29:20,550
Jaguar, you're the biggest
threat to the Ardientes.

551
00:29:20,633 --> 00:29:22,343
Will you let this traitor lie to you?

552
00:29:23,511 --> 00:29:25,430
Don't believe him! He's lying!

553
00:29:26,014 --> 00:29:27,182
You're a liar!

554
00:29:28,099 --> 00:29:30,602
-Give me your gun!
-Jaguar, he's a liar.

555
00:29:31,144 --> 00:29:33,313
I saw him talking to Julio Ardiente.

556
00:29:33,396 --> 00:29:35,440
-Now, you decide.
-[Rufo] Give me your gun!

557
00:29:36,274 --> 00:29:38,526
Give me your gun! Oh, come on!

558
00:29:41,196 --> 00:29:42,197
-You!
-Jaguar.

559
00:29:42,280 --> 00:29:44,741
Give me your gun! Let's kill him!

560
00:29:45,158 --> 00:29:46,451
[Rufo] Give it to me!

561
00:29:46,868 --> 00:29:48,203
What's wrong with you?!

562
00:29:48,787 --> 00:29:50,413
Give me a gun!

563
00:29:50,997 --> 00:29:52,832
Come on! Jaguar…

564
00:29:53,500 --> 00:29:54,626
Jaguar…

565
00:29:55,960 --> 00:29:56,961
Don't.

566
00:29:57,629 --> 00:29:59,839
Please don't, Jaguar.

567
00:30:01,299 --> 00:30:03,635
Don't, Jaguar. Please…

568
00:30:03,718 --> 00:30:06,012
[tense music playing]

569
00:30:10,391 --> 00:30:12,018
-[gunshot]
-[Rufo groaning]

570
00:30:14,813 --> 00:30:17,899
[Rufo groaning]

571
00:30:25,824 --> 00:30:28,409
Jaguar, if I were you, I'd finish him off

572
00:30:28,493 --> 00:30:30,370
before he becomes an asset
to the Ardientes.

573
00:30:30,703 --> 00:30:33,289
[tense music playing]

574
00:30:40,672 --> 00:30:43,633
The boss is asking what reward you want:

575
00:30:43,716 --> 00:30:45,176
money or weapons?

576
00:30:45,260 --> 00:30:47,720
[tense music playing]

577
00:30:50,181 --> 00:30:51,808
I want to be part of your group.

578
00:31:01,150 --> 00:31:02,110
[grunts]

579
00:31:05,530 --> 00:31:06,656
[grunts]

580
00:31:06,739 --> 00:31:08,908
[tense music playing]

581
00:31:12,579 --> 00:31:14,414
[groans]

582
00:31:16,207 --> 00:31:17,208
[chokes]

583
00:31:19,544 --> 00:31:22,630
Stop it! Enough, Jaguar!

584
00:31:23,631 --> 00:31:24,757
Please stop.

585
00:31:24,841 --> 00:31:27,635
Have mercy on me, please.

586
00:31:29,178 --> 00:31:32,682
Do you know what I do
to traitors like you?

587
00:31:34,017 --> 00:31:35,476
I cut them in half.

588
00:31:35,560 --> 00:31:37,353
[sobbing]

589
00:31:38,688 --> 00:31:39,981
Jaguar, no!

590
00:31:41,274 --> 00:31:42,483
[chainsaw starts]

591
00:31:42,567 --> 00:31:44,485
[screams]

592
00:31:48,364 --> 00:31:51,868
No, Jaguar! I'm begging you!

593
00:31:51,951 --> 00:31:53,494
[screaming and sobbing]

594
00:31:53,578 --> 00:31:54,621
Here.

595
00:31:55,997 --> 00:31:57,373
Your boss is looking for you.

596
00:31:58,708 --> 00:32:00,209
This is what I'll do.

597
00:32:00,710 --> 00:32:03,004
I'll send him half of your body.

598
00:32:03,087 --> 00:32:04,631
[sobbing]

599
00:32:06,215 --> 00:32:09,052
-No!
-Listen, all of you!

600
00:32:09,427 --> 00:32:11,638
Don't you even try to copy this bastard!

601
00:32:12,013 --> 00:32:13,723
Don't do what this traitor did.

602
00:32:13,806 --> 00:32:15,099
Do you understand?!

603
00:32:15,433 --> 00:32:17,518
Boss, what about Madrigal?

604
00:32:17,602 --> 00:32:19,020
Can we trust him?

605
00:32:21,189 --> 00:32:23,441
Have mercy, Jaguar!

606
00:32:26,277 --> 00:32:27,403
Ivy?

607
00:32:29,864 --> 00:32:30,865
Ivy!

608
00:32:30,949 --> 00:32:33,159
[suspenseful music playing]

609
00:32:35,203 --> 00:32:37,246
[Arthur] <i>You might not reach her alive.</i>

610
00:32:37,538 --> 00:32:42,543
<i>You and Ivy Aguas</i>
<i>will be reunited in hell.</i>

611
00:32:42,627 --> 00:32:43,628
<i>He lied to me.</i>

612
00:32:43,711 --> 00:32:45,463
-[whimpers]
-Ivy?

613
00:32:46,881 --> 00:32:48,716
-[muffled screams]
-Ivy?

614
00:32:50,718 --> 00:32:52,720
Ivy. Wait, wait.

615
00:32:52,804 --> 00:32:54,138
Come on.

616
00:32:54,889 --> 00:32:57,308
-[muffled crying]
-It's okay. I'm here.

617
00:32:58,726 --> 00:32:59,852
[sobbing]

618
00:32:59,936 --> 00:33:02,522
Don't cry, I'm here.

619
00:33:02,605 --> 00:33:04,065
[sobbing continues]

620
00:33:05,525 --> 00:33:07,318
Don't cry. It's okay.

621
00:33:07,402 --> 00:33:10,613
I'm here. I'm here. I'm here.
It's okay. Calm down.

622
00:33:10,697 --> 00:33:12,407
[sobbing]

623
00:33:12,490 --> 00:33:14,200
Don't cry. It's okay.

624
00:33:14,283 --> 00:33:15,743
It's okay now.

625
00:33:16,619 --> 00:33:18,579
That bastard, what did he do to you?

626
00:33:18,663 --> 00:33:20,999
[sobbing]

627
00:33:21,082 --> 00:33:23,584
[tense music playing]

628
00:33:30,883 --> 00:33:33,428
I'm here. I'm here.

629
00:33:35,263 --> 00:33:36,639
[sobbing]

630
00:33:36,723 --> 00:33:38,558
You're safe now. You're safe now.

631
00:33:38,641 --> 00:33:42,145
-No.
-You're safe now. I'm here.

632
00:33:43,104 --> 00:33:44,605
Ivy, I'm here.

633
00:33:44,689 --> 00:33:45,732
It's Arnaldo.

634
00:33:46,858 --> 00:33:49,068
I'm here. They're gone.

635
00:33:49,152 --> 00:33:52,488
It's just me here. It's okay now.

636
00:33:52,572 --> 00:33:53,656
I'm here. Don't worry.

637
00:33:53,740 --> 00:33:56,617
Hon, who was that?

638
00:33:56,701 --> 00:33:59,203
Why did he kidnap me?

639
00:34:01,748 --> 00:34:03,082
I'm sorry.

640
00:34:04,083 --> 00:34:07,128
Forgive me. This is all my fault.

641
00:34:07,211 --> 00:34:09,922
-Forgive me.
-Our engagement ring…

642
00:34:10,006 --> 00:34:11,716
-He took it!
-It's with me! It's here!

643
00:34:11,799 --> 00:34:13,134
No, it's with him!

644
00:34:13,217 --> 00:34:16,471
It's here! It's here!
I have it! I have it.

645
00:34:16,554 --> 00:34:18,931
-[sobbing]
-I have it.

646
00:34:19,015 --> 00:34:20,349
It's all right.

647
00:34:20,433 --> 00:34:22,435
Stop crying. We're safe now.

648
00:34:22,518 --> 00:34:27,482
He said I should be careful around you.

649
00:34:28,524 --> 00:34:31,194
He said I shouldn't go near you.

650
00:34:31,277 --> 00:34:33,529
Why? What did you do to him?

651
00:34:33,613 --> 00:34:35,323
What did you do, hon?

652
00:34:36,365 --> 00:34:38,284
[Arnaldo] <i>I can easily</i>
<i>kill you if I wanted to.</i>

653
00:34:38,367 --> 00:34:40,912
<i>And I can make it look like</i>
<i>you committed suicide</i>

654
00:34:40,995 --> 00:34:43,581
<i>just like what I did to Carlotta.</i>

655
00:34:43,998 --> 00:34:47,085
<i>Or I can also pin the blame</i>
<i>on someone else,</i>

656
00:34:47,168 --> 00:34:49,962
<i>just like I framed Diego</i>
<i>when I killed Nimfa.</i>

657
00:34:54,008 --> 00:34:55,718
I… I don't know. I don't remember.

658
00:34:55,802 --> 00:34:57,762
I can't even recall his face.

659
00:34:58,429 --> 00:35:02,558
All I know is that he's crazy.
But don't be scared.

660
00:35:02,642 --> 00:35:06,187
Don't think about that, okay?
Don't believe him, okay?

661
00:35:06,270 --> 00:35:07,480
I won't do anything bad to you.

662
00:35:07,563 --> 00:35:09,899
[stammers] I will never hurt you.

663
00:35:09,982 --> 00:35:12,235
Okay? I'm here. You're safe now.

664
00:35:12,318 --> 00:35:13,611
Okay?

665
00:35:13,694 --> 00:35:17,657
Stop crying. Stop crying. Stop crying.

666
00:35:17,740 --> 00:35:20,034
No one can hurt you anymore.

667
00:35:20,118 --> 00:35:21,953
I won't let anything happen to you again.

668
00:35:22,703 --> 00:35:24,413
-[sniffles]
-Okay?

669
00:35:24,497 --> 00:35:25,998
Stop crying.

670
00:35:26,082 --> 00:35:28,626
Let's go home. Let's go home.

671
00:35:28,709 --> 00:35:30,878
I'll have a doctor see you too.

672
00:35:31,796 --> 00:35:33,005
Okay?

673
00:35:33,089 --> 00:35:33,881
Let's go home.

674
00:35:34,674 --> 00:35:35,675
Let's go.

675
00:35:36,300 --> 00:35:37,635
Can you stand?

676
00:35:39,095 --> 00:35:40,721
Slowly. Slowly.

677
00:35:40,805 --> 00:35:43,432
[suspenseful music playing]

678
00:35:50,565 --> 00:35:52,775
-Hon, is he really gone?
-He's gone.

679
00:35:52,859 --> 00:35:54,735
What if he's still here?

680
00:35:58,739 --> 00:36:01,200
[suspenseful music playing]

681
00:36:14,005 --> 00:36:15,047
Papa.

682
00:36:15,381 --> 00:36:17,967
So, your informant's not responding, eh?

683
00:36:19,010 --> 00:36:22,221
Maybe Jaguar has already intercepted him.

684
00:36:22,889 --> 00:36:25,016
You know, I really have
a strong feeling, Papa.

685
00:36:25,099 --> 00:36:26,392
He's really watching us.

686
00:36:26,475 --> 00:36:28,519
Shut up, Emilia!

687
00:36:28,603 --> 00:36:30,771
Keep your trap shut

688
00:36:30,855 --> 00:36:35,902
before I take all my anger
at Jaguar out on you!

689
00:36:36,569 --> 00:36:39,655
That's not fair at all, Papa!
You're too harsh!

690
00:36:40,198 --> 00:36:42,700
You're such a sore loser.
Don't worry, Papa.

691
00:36:42,783 --> 00:36:45,286
We can still get our revenge
on that Jaguar.

692
00:36:45,369 --> 00:36:50,416
For your information, I am not a loser.

693
00:36:51,834 --> 00:36:54,962
Yeah, Papa, but the score still stands.

694
00:36:55,046 --> 00:36:57,215
Jaguar, one.

695
00:36:57,298 --> 00:36:58,883
Julio, zero.

696
00:37:00,301 --> 00:37:01,802
Is that your new job?

697
00:37:01,886 --> 00:37:04,222
Are you a sports statistician now?

698
00:37:04,305 --> 00:37:05,765
You're keeping scores on us?

699
00:37:06,515 --> 00:37:07,391
[scoffs]

700
00:37:07,475 --> 00:37:09,143
I can see it! You're smirking!

701
00:37:09,227 --> 00:37:11,312
You want to laugh at me
because I'm losing.

702
00:37:11,395 --> 00:37:13,105
Are you glad that I'm losing?!

703
00:37:13,648 --> 00:37:15,233
-Hmm?
-Is that the case?

704
00:37:15,316 --> 00:37:17,735
[tense music playing]

705
00:37:17,818 --> 00:37:20,655
I will prove to you that the person

706
00:37:20,738 --> 00:37:22,990
who can defeat Julio Ardiente
is yet to be born.

707
00:37:23,074 --> 00:37:25,284
[suspenseful music playing]

708
00:37:25,368 --> 00:37:26,535
[line rings]

709
00:37:27,411 --> 00:37:28,371
It's me.

710
00:37:28,996 --> 00:37:30,623
I want you to do me a favor.

711
00:37:30,706 --> 00:37:33,918
I want you to mount a manhunt

712
00:37:34,001 --> 00:37:36,587
against this hoodlum Jaguar.

713
00:37:38,923 --> 00:37:41,259
I want you to find him, catch him…

714
00:37:42,009 --> 00:37:43,219
and kill him.

715
00:37:43,719 --> 00:37:45,471
ASAP.

716
00:37:46,222 --> 00:37:48,057
Yes, please. Do me that favor.

717
00:37:48,641 --> 00:37:50,226
I want you to end his life.

718
00:37:51,435 --> 00:37:52,687
Now…

719
00:37:52,770 --> 00:37:55,898
Let's see what that Jaguar
will do once he learns

720
00:37:55,982 --> 00:37:59,485
that the police aren't
the only ones after him…

721
00:37:59,568 --> 00:38:02,196
but a whole private army.

722
00:38:04,073 --> 00:38:06,075
Papa, you really are mad.

723
00:38:06,158 --> 00:38:07,743
I'm not just mad.

724
00:38:08,202 --> 00:38:10,496
My blood is curdling from fury.

725
00:38:10,579 --> 00:38:14,125
And I promise you, I will make
that Jaguar lose his manhood.

726
00:38:14,208 --> 00:38:17,086
[tense music playing]

727
00:38:30,141 --> 00:38:31,267
This is from the boss.

728
00:38:32,351 --> 00:38:34,937
[ominous music playing]

729
00:38:39,066 --> 00:38:40,484
[phone rings]

730
00:38:43,070 --> 00:38:44,613
[ringing continues]

731
00:38:46,324 --> 00:38:48,451
-Boss.
-Welcome to my group.

732
00:38:49,160 --> 00:38:51,662
From now on, that will be your uniform.

733
00:38:53,581 --> 00:38:55,207
But there's one thing I'll ask of you.

734
00:38:55,291 --> 00:38:56,792
[distorted voice] <i>I hope you can do it.</i>

735
00:38:58,502 --> 00:39:00,171
I just want you to be loyal to me.

736
00:39:02,423 --> 00:39:06,302
And you'll get everything you want.

737
00:39:06,385 --> 00:39:07,678
I hear you loud and clear, boss.

738
00:39:08,763 --> 00:39:09,889
Very good.

739
00:39:11,015 --> 00:39:13,351
Wait for my next call.

740
00:39:13,809 --> 00:39:15,644
I have a task for you.

741
00:39:16,020 --> 00:39:18,647
[suspenseful music playing]

742
00:39:42,421 --> 00:39:45,007
[somber music playing]

743
00:39:49,178 --> 00:39:50,221
Hon?

744
00:39:50,304 --> 00:39:52,723
You can't look this way, okay?

745
00:39:53,891 --> 00:39:56,894
We need to fix you up.
Appear as if nothing happened.

746
00:39:57,603 --> 00:40:00,064
I don't want Grandpa to see you like this,

747
00:40:00,147 --> 00:40:03,401
because the election stress
is taking a toll on him,

748
00:40:03,484 --> 00:40:05,069
and I don't want to add to that.

749
00:40:05,152 --> 00:40:06,362
Is that okay?

750
00:40:07,196 --> 00:40:09,532
Can we pretend as if nothing happened?

751
00:40:11,283 --> 00:40:14,078
Can we do that? I'm sorry
if I'm asking too much.

752
00:40:15,079 --> 00:40:16,372
It's okay, hon.

753
00:40:17,373 --> 00:40:18,457
Okay.

754
00:40:19,208 --> 00:40:20,251
Okay.

755
00:40:20,334 --> 00:40:22,878
[somber music playing]

756
00:40:24,171 --> 00:40:25,381
What?

757
00:40:27,716 --> 00:40:28,801
Thank you.

758
00:40:31,637 --> 00:40:33,180
[sobbing]

759
00:40:36,517 --> 00:40:38,894
[sniffles] Thanks, hon.

760
00:40:41,730 --> 00:40:43,232
Thank you.

761
00:40:45,943 --> 00:40:48,612
Thank you for saving me.

762
00:40:50,489 --> 00:40:52,867
When I was locked up,

763
00:40:52,950 --> 00:40:54,410
while I was locked up, hon,

764
00:40:54,493 --> 00:40:56,662
when he was hurting me,

765
00:40:56,745 --> 00:41:00,082
when he told me that
he was going to kill me,

766
00:41:00,166 --> 00:41:01,625
I was so scared!

767
00:41:02,751 --> 00:41:05,504
I was so scared that I'd die,

768
00:41:05,588 --> 00:41:07,423
that we'd never get married.

769
00:41:07,506 --> 00:41:09,717
That I'd never be with you anymore.

770
00:41:10,217 --> 00:41:11,927
So, thank you, hon.

771
00:41:13,387 --> 00:41:15,347
Thank you for saving me.

772
00:41:16,015 --> 00:41:18,309
I'm sorry it took longer.

773
00:41:18,851 --> 00:41:19,685
[sniffles]

774
00:41:19,768 --> 00:41:21,979
I'm sorry I took too long.

775
00:41:22,605 --> 00:41:25,608
When you were gone,
I didn't know what to do.

776
00:41:25,691 --> 00:41:27,985
I couldn't imagine a life without you.

777
00:41:28,402 --> 00:41:29,403
Hon.

778
00:41:31,822 --> 00:41:33,616
I don't think I could take it.

779
00:41:35,493 --> 00:41:37,036
What if we get married right away?

780
00:41:39,205 --> 00:41:41,040
Let's get married soon-- Sooner.

781
00:41:42,291 --> 00:41:44,585
I want to marry you sooner.

782
00:41:44,668 --> 00:41:45,878
-Yes.
-I want to prove to everyone

783
00:41:45,961 --> 00:41:47,671
that they can't go against our love.

784
00:41:47,755 --> 00:41:49,924
They can't break what we have.

785
00:41:50,007 --> 00:41:52,218
-Let's get married sooner.
-Yes.

786
00:41:52,301 --> 00:41:53,219
Next week.

787
00:41:53,302 --> 00:41:54,303
Yes.

788
00:41:54,386 --> 00:41:56,013
Yes, hon.

789
00:41:56,096 --> 00:41:57,556
Yes, please.

790
00:41:57,640 --> 00:42:00,184
[tense music playing]

791
00:42:05,481 --> 00:42:07,274
I won't let anyone hurt you.

792
00:42:11,487 --> 00:42:12,863
Prepare the guest room, hurry.

793
00:42:12,947 --> 00:42:15,032
Arnaldo? What happened?

794
00:42:15,115 --> 00:42:17,117
Grandpa, I think she got food poisoning

795
00:42:17,201 --> 00:42:19,119
from the restaurant where we had our date.

796
00:42:19,203 --> 00:42:20,621
Are you sure?

797
00:42:20,704 --> 00:42:22,414
Yeah. I'm sure.

798
00:42:22,498 --> 00:42:24,708
The doctor's on his way. We'll go now.

799
00:42:25,084 --> 00:42:27,836
[unsettling music playing]

800
00:42:36,720 --> 00:42:37,805
Anna…

801
00:42:39,056 --> 00:42:42,351
I can't calm down until
I speak to my daughter.

802
00:42:43,727 --> 00:42:47,606
What if Ivy's with Jepoy?

803
00:42:47,982 --> 00:42:49,775
Do you know anything about Lily's plan?

804
00:42:50,776 --> 00:42:54,989
No, but Jepoy told me
he's going to find a way

805
00:42:55,072 --> 00:42:57,533
to stop Ivy and Arnaldo's wedding.

806
00:43:00,369 --> 00:43:01,412
There's Jepoy.

807
00:43:01,495 --> 00:43:03,122
Jepoy, where have you been?

808
00:43:03,497 --> 00:43:06,000
Observing the Ardientes. Why?

809
00:43:06,083 --> 00:43:07,501
-Jepoy…
-Ma'am?

810
00:43:07,585 --> 00:43:09,253
Did you see Lily there?

811
00:43:10,212 --> 00:43:11,422
She wasn't there.

812
00:43:13,007 --> 00:43:14,508
Did something happen to her?

813
00:43:14,592 --> 00:43:16,677
[ominous music playing]

814
00:43:20,264 --> 00:43:24,018
Other than early signs
of dehydration and fatigue,

815
00:43:24,101 --> 00:43:25,477
your fiancée is okay.

816
00:43:26,604 --> 00:43:27,771
Thanks, doc.

817
00:43:28,272 --> 00:43:29,648
Um, doc?

818
00:43:30,274 --> 00:43:33,569
Can you please check
my daughter-in-law thoroughly?

819
00:43:33,652 --> 00:43:36,614
She might be suffering from
"overacting syndrome"

820
00:43:36,697 --> 00:43:39,742
or "dramatictitis." Don't you think?

821
00:43:39,825 --> 00:43:40,868
[Arnaldo] Mom!

822
00:43:42,369 --> 00:43:43,537
[doctor] Excuse me.

823
00:43:44,455 --> 00:43:45,748
I'm just concerned.

824
00:43:45,831 --> 00:43:47,833
You don't look concerned.

825
00:43:48,626 --> 00:43:50,794
You're no stranger to
plotting against Ivy's life.

826
00:43:50,878 --> 00:43:53,130
Did you have anything to do with this?

827
00:43:53,213 --> 00:43:56,884
Hey! You, young man,
don't talk to me that way.

828
00:43:56,967 --> 00:43:58,510
How dare you?

829
00:43:58,594 --> 00:44:00,804
Don't pin this on me.
I had nothing to do with this.

830
00:44:00,888 --> 00:44:02,139
Then why are you--

831
00:44:02,222 --> 00:44:03,515
Oh, shut up!

832
00:44:05,726 --> 00:44:06,977
-[exhales]
-[Arnaldo] Sorry.

833
00:44:08,937 --> 00:44:09,980
Sorry.

834
00:44:10,064 --> 00:44:12,524
[unsettling music playing]

835
00:44:15,486 --> 00:44:17,988
You must forgive your mother.

836
00:44:18,072 --> 00:44:19,782
She has this weird spell,

837
00:44:19,865 --> 00:44:24,036
especially when there's a full moon out.

838
00:44:24,119 --> 00:44:25,204
[chuckles]

839
00:44:25,287 --> 00:44:28,082
Anyway, you two rest. Okay?

840
00:44:29,208 --> 00:44:30,459
Grandpa?

841
00:44:31,627 --> 00:44:32,586
Before you leave,

842
00:44:32,670 --> 00:44:34,963
Ivy and I want to tell you something.

843
00:44:36,882 --> 00:44:37,966
What is it?

844
00:44:39,426 --> 00:44:40,844
Well, we want to…

845
00:44:41,261 --> 00:44:43,222
we want our wedding to happen soon.

846
00:44:45,849 --> 00:44:47,017
How soon?

847
00:44:49,478 --> 00:44:50,437
Next week.

848
00:44:53,148 --> 00:44:54,483
Next week…

849
00:44:57,277 --> 00:44:58,987
We can make that happen.

850
00:44:59,530 --> 00:45:01,281
Next week will be good.

851
00:45:01,949 --> 00:45:02,866
I'm okay with that.

852
00:45:04,451 --> 00:45:05,911
Truth of the matter is,

853
00:45:05,994 --> 00:45:09,248
I can't wait to see you get married.

854
00:45:12,418 --> 00:45:13,335
-Wonderful.
-Thank you.

855
00:45:13,419 --> 00:45:14,837
Thank you, Congressman.

856
00:45:14,920 --> 00:45:17,089
You're very welcome, Miss Aguas.

857
00:45:17,631 --> 00:45:18,549
And don't worry.

858
00:45:19,383 --> 00:45:21,343
I will make sure that nothing

859
00:45:21,427 --> 00:45:23,095
will get in the way of your wedding.

860
00:45:26,223 --> 00:45:27,349
Now get some rest.

861
00:45:27,433 --> 00:45:28,767
Thank you, Grandpa.

862
00:45:28,851 --> 00:45:31,395
[ominous music playing]

863
00:45:45,701 --> 00:45:48,328
<i>We have been preparing for the forthcoming</i>

864
00:45:48,412 --> 00:45:51,540
<i>Aguas-Ardiente royal wedding.</i>

865
00:45:51,623 --> 00:45:56,211
<i>It is finally going to happen</i>
<i>a week from today.</i>

866
00:45:56,295 --> 00:45:58,922
<i>No! No! No! No!</i>

867
00:45:59,006 --> 00:46:00,424
[Arnaldo] <i>You think</i>
<i>I don't know what you did?</i>

868
00:46:00,507 --> 00:46:01,925
<i>You had Arthur kidnap Ivy.</i>

869
00:46:02,009 --> 00:46:04,011
<i>You can't stop our wedding!</i>

870
00:46:04,094 --> 00:46:07,639
<i>I'll put a stop to all your plans.</i>

871
00:46:07,723 --> 00:46:08,891
<i>No!</i>

872
00:46:09,808 --> 00:46:11,768
[Jepoy] <i>Now that I have money and weapons,</i>

873
00:46:11,852 --> 00:46:15,481
<i>I will stop your wedding</i>
<i>with bullets, Arnaldo.</i>

874
00:46:18,025 --> 00:46:21,653
[theme music playing]
